{
    "background_story": "In a small pond near the Russian countryside, a duckling named Duckling lived a humble life. One day, while swimming near the water's edge, he stumbled upon a tattered book of Maxim Gorky's stories. Enchanted by the writer's vivid descriptions of the human condition, Duckling became obsessed with the author's works. As he waddled around the pond, he'd often quote Gorky's famous phrases to his fellow ducks, who'd quack in confusion. Despite their teasing, Duckling continued to read and learn, finding solace in Gorky's words about perseverance and the struggle for a better life. He even started a small book club, where he'd read aloud to his fellow waterfowl, inspiring them to see the world beyond their pond. Duckling's love for Gorky's literature transformed him into a unlikely intellectual, earning him the nickname 'The Quacking Philosopher'.",
